From 9c1e2c798138760e5410d7d9ddcc9e3fea1f6d24 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 11:05:34 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] Vercel: close stuck runs, faster Firebase lookups

- Cancel now closes a run that no server is running any more (past its time limit),
  and /cron/run-schedules marks such runs failed instead of leaving them Running.
- Firestore uses REST (preferRest): no slow gRPC start-up on each Vercel cold start.
- Firebase lookup steps read 10 documents at a time instead of one by one.
- Scheduled runs show 'Schedule' instead of 'External (webhook)'.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Way2MU7LHJAr1mxzSsa49C
